1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
Subs by Mkrm

2
00:01:28,840 --> 00:01:30,780
What's the point of crying now?

3
00:01:31,040 --> 00:01:31,710
It's all trouble caused by desire.

4
00:01:32,160 --> 00:01:34,140
Whatever problems you have, that's not my concern.

5
00:01:35,080 --> 00:01:36,540
Coach, what kind of trouble are we in?

6
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:37,470
Coach Tony.

7
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:37,950
Coach Tony.

8
00:01:37,960 --> 00:01:39,420
And you are?

9
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:40,830
If Monica's Mom

10
00:01:40,840 --> 00:01:41,820
keeps hovering around watching us train,

11
00:01:42,560 --> 00:01:44,700
there's no way we'll be able to get any real practice done.

12
00:01:45,000 --> 00:01:46,620
Monica, you came to see me, right?

13
00:01:47,080 --> 00:01:49,020
I... I wanted to ask you guys for a favor.

14
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:51,420
You're always off by yourself, away from everyone else.

15
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:53,820
Is it to find your feel for the Yo-Yo?

16
00:01:56,000 --> 00:01:59,500
Episode 10

17
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:08,220
Ah! Help!

18
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,660
It's this room! It's this one!

19
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:13,980
Help! Oh my god, help!

20
00:02:14,440 --> 00:02:15,420
Oh god, help!

21
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:17,820
What's wrong?

22
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,700
Under the bed... there's a...

23
00:02:21,160 --> 00:02:22,140
There's a what?

24
00:02:22,880 --> 00:02:24,540
Is it a mouse?

25
00:02:25,480 --> 00:02:26,460
A mouse?

26
00:02:26,720 --> 00:02:28,860
Whoa! So many little ducklings!

27
00:02:33,160 --> 00:02:35,580
Ah! Oh my god!

28
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:39,900
Don't be scared! They're just ducklings, not mice!

29
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:43,740
Quick! Get them out of here! Chase them away!

30
00:02:44,200 --> 00:02:45,660
Please! I'm begging you!

31
00:02:46,120 --> 00:02:47,580
Aww, what adorable little ducklings!

32
00:02:48,520 --> 00:02:49,500
They're so cute and fluffy!

33
00:02:50,040 --> 00:02:50,940
No! No!

34
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:51,900
Maybe we should just take these ducklings...

35
00:02:52,840 --> 00:02:53,820
and return them to their mother.

36
00:02:57,160 --> 00:03:00,540
H-How can you be afraid of ducklings?

37
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:02,940
Just get them out! Chase them away!

38
00:03:03,680 --> 00:03:05,340
I'm packing my bags! I'm going home!

39
00:03:06,380 --> 00:03:06,880
I'm going home!

40
00:03:07,920 --> 00:03:08,700
Okay, okay, okay.

41
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,000
You are a grown adult.

42
00:03:14,440 --> 00:03:16,860
How could anyone be afraid of these adorable,
innocent little ducklings?

43
00:03:17,320 --> 00:03:18,300
Don't say another word.

44
00:03:18,760 --> 00:03:21,180
I want to go home! I want to go home!

45
00:03:25,960 --> 00:03:28,860
This is how she was acting. "No! No!"

46
00:03:29,320 --> 00:03:30,780
"I want to go home! I want to go home!"

47
00:03:33,640 --> 00:03:34,620
Can we come up?

48
00:03:35,560 --> 00:03:37,020
Come on up! Hurry, hurry!

49
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:42,780
Coach! Coach!

50
00:03:43,240 --> 00:03:43,740
Still awake?

51
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:45,180
Let's chat for a bit.

52
00:03:45,200 --> 00:03:46,000
Yeah.

53
00:03:46,500 --> 00:03:47,580
Coach, have a seat.

54
00:03:48,040 --> 00:03:49,020
What were you all laughing about just now?

55
00:03:49,080 --> 00:03:50,460
We were laughing about Ms. Marilyn.

56
00:03:50,920 --> 00:03:52,860
Show some respect. That's Monica's Mother.

57
00:03:56,200 --> 00:03:58,620
Coach, Monica's mom actually left.

58
00:04:02,440 --> 00:04:02,940
I still don't get it.

59
00:04:03,880 --> 00:04:04,860
Tell me. How can a grown woman

60
00:04:05,320 --> 00:04:06,780
be afraid of little ducklings?

61
00:04:07,520 --> 00:04:09,660
Coach, aren't you afraid of mice?

62
00:04:11,740 --> 00:04:12,540
How did you know that?

63
00:04:13,180 --> 00:04:15,420
When I said there might be a mouse under the bed earlier,

64
00:04:15,880 --> 00:04:17,340
you jumped back like 3 steps!

65
00:04:21,440 --> 00:04:22,620
Being afraid of mice is totally normal.

66
00:04:22,880 --> 00:04:24,060
Lots of people are afraid of mice.

67
00:04:24,520 --> 00:04:26,230
But I have never, ever heard of anyone
being afraid of little ducklings.

68
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:27,900
Me? I'm not afraid of mice.

69
00:04:28,440 --> 00:04:30,780
We're not afraid of mice, either.

70
00:04:32,680 --> 00:04:33,660
No way, you guys?

71
00:04:34,120 --> 00:04:36,060
My absolute favorite is Jerry.

72
00:04:36,520 --> 00:04:38,460
And I love Mickey Mouse in the cartoons.

73
00:04:39,400 --> 00:04:40,380
Those don't count.

74
00:04:40,820 --> 00:04:43,740
Those are just idealized, romanticized versions of mice in movies.

75
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,620
But they really are cute, though.

76
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:49,500
Their little see-through ears, their tiny mouths...

77
00:04:49,660 --> 00:04:50,460
Alright, alright, that's enough!

78
00:04:51,880 --> 00:04:55,740
The next person who describes a mouse to me

79
00:04:56,200 --> 00:04:57,180
is getting kicked off the Team!

80
00:05:00,520 --> 00:05:03,420
So, is there any little animal that you guys are scared of?

81
00:05:03,880 --> 00:05:07,260
Yeah. I'm terrified of cockroaches.

82
00:05:07,720 --> 00:05:09,660
Yeah, cockroaches are the worst.

83
00:05:11,080 --> 00:05:12,540
I'm most afraid of caterpillars.

84
00:05:13,660 --> 00:05:14,940
Leo, what about you?

85
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:17,340
I'm scared of lizards.

86
00:05:18,280 --> 00:05:19,260
I'm scared of spiders.

87
00:05:19,720 --> 00:05:22,140
The scariest thing in the entire world is snakes.

88
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,950
All those things you guys mentioned,

89
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,600
I've actually heard of people being scared of them.

90
00:05:28,540 --> 00:05:30,300
But this is genuinely the first time in my life

91
00:05:30,760 --> 00:05:32,220
I've ever heard of someone being afraid of ducklings.

92
00:05:35,060 --> 00:05:36,940
My Mom's had anatidaephobia (fear of ducks)
ever since she was a kid.

93
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:37,950
Not just live ducks, either.

94
00:05:37,960 --> 00:05:39,900
Even roasted duck, braised duck, salted duck...

95
00:05:40,340 --> 00:05:41,340
she stays away from all of it.

96
00:05:45,160 --> 00:05:46,620
So that's why we got the idea

97
00:05:47,080 --> 00:05:48,720
to put those ducklings under her bed.

98
00:05:49,660 --> 00:05:50,460
What?

99
00:05:52,060 --> 00:05:52,860
You guys did this?

100
00:05:53,320 --> 00:05:55,260
Well, Monica was the one who
came to us and asked for our help.

101
00:05:56,000 --> 00:05:57,180
If she hadn't told us,

102
00:05:57,340 --> 00:05:59,580
how would we ever have known her Mom was terrified of ducks?

103
00:06:01,080 --> 00:06:03,420
I admit my Mom can be a bit much sometimes.

104
00:06:04,360 --> 00:06:06,780
But I figured our Training was just way more important.

105
00:06:11,080 --> 00:06:13,020
That wasn't a very nice thing for you guys to do.

106
00:06:14,440 --> 00:06:17,340
Well, luckily, it was only Monica's mom.

107
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:18,270
If it had been me,

108
00:06:18,280 --> 00:06:20,220
I wouldn't be scared of some silly little ducklings.

109
00:06:20,680 --> 00:06:22,590
I mean, ducklings are so adorable!

110
00:06:22,600 --> 00:06:25,020
With their fluffy little heads and
those big, bright, curious eyes,

111
00:06:25,180 --> 00:06:26,240
looking all around...

112
00:06:27,480 --> 00:06:28,380
Coach?

113
00:06:29,320 --> 00:06:30,820
Ah!

114
00:06:40,160 --> 00:06:41,210
Alright, everyone, let's take a break.

115
00:06:48,200 --> 00:06:49,500
Coach has been acting so weird lately.

116
00:06:50,920 --> 00:06:52,860
He's always running off to Manager Ma's office.

117
00:06:53,320 --> 00:06:54,780
Why do you care what the Coach does so much?

118
00:06:55,620 --> 00:06:57,920
As long as Mark's here to manage things, isn't that enough?

119
00:07:12,700 --> 00:07:13,800
Leo's always sneaking off

120
00:07:13,810 --> 00:07:14,950
to practice by himself.

121
00:07:15,880 --> 00:07:16,380
So shady.

122
00:07:18,280 --> 00:07:20,700
Well, the best Players are usually a little bit different, right?

123
00:07:21,160 --> 00:07:24,060
Leo says he prefers being alone when he's
trying to find his feel for the Yo-Yo.

124
00:07:25,480 --> 00:07:26,460
What kind of "Best Player"

125
00:07:27,400 --> 00:07:28,860
is too scared to even bust a move against someone?

126
00:07:29,800 --> 00:07:30,300
If you ask me,

127
00:07:30,760 --> 00:07:32,210
he's nothing more than a show-off.

128
00:07:36,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Leo.

129
00:07:37,760 --> 00:07:39,150
Who gave you permission to go off and train by yourself?

130
00:07:40,840 --> 00:07:41,820
Didn't the Coach say

131
00:07:42,280 --> 00:07:43,740
that we should all split up and start figuring out

132
00:07:44,200 --> 00:07:45,180
our own Signature Moves?

133
00:07:45,640 --> 00:07:47,960
That doesn't mean you get to just isolate
yourself from the rest of the Team.

134
00:07:53,600 --> 00:07:54,300
I'm not isolating myself.

135
00:07:55,720 --> 00:07:56,700
I'm just practicing a little farther away from everyone.

136
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:58,620
Everyone else is training together.

137
00:07:59,360 --> 00:08:00,940
But you always have to go off on your own.

138
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:02,460
Like you're so special or something.

139
00:08:03,880 --> 00:08:04,860
Hmph. What's so special about him?

140
00:08:05,800 --> 00:08:08,700
He's just the Runner-Up from some Tournament in America.

141
00:08:09,720 --> 00:08:10,970
You can disagree with my Training Methods

142
00:08:10,980 --> 00:08:12,060
all you want,

143
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:13,780
But please, don't make it personal.

144
00:08:14,520 --> 00:08:15,870
I'm not making it personal.

145
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:16,450
You are just a Runner-Up.

146
00:08:17,800 --> 00:08:20,700
In my eyes, a Runner-Up is nothing but a Loser.

147
00:08:21,640 --> 00:08:24,060
They can never, ever be mentioned
in the same breath as a Champion.

148
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:26,940
No matter what Tournament you're the Champion of,

149
00:08:27,580 --> 00:08:29,820
this "Loser" right here will still beat you.

150
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:31,000
Huh!

151
00:08:31,240 --> 00:08:32,700
Finally, you're stepping up to the plate.

152
00:08:33,160 --> 00:08:35,250
I was starting to think you'd just
hide in your turtle shell forever.

153
00:08:36,220 --> 00:08:37,980
Tomorrow morning, fishing platform.

154
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:39,770
Don't chicken out.

155
00:08:41,500 --> 00:08:42,300
And once I beat you,

156
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,660
you will never, ever mention the word "Runner-Up"

157
00:08:46,120 --> 00:08:47,580
in front of me ever again.

158
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,020
Deal.

159
00:09:11,560 --> 00:09:12,060
Sis.

160
00:09:12,520 --> 00:09:14,460
They're finally gonna see just how good Leo really is.

161
00:09:15,200 --> 00:09:16,860
Keep your voice down.

162
00:09:24,700 --> 00:09:26,940
Popcorn, who do you think's gonna win this match?

163
00:09:27,880 --> 00:09:30,780
Win or lose, it doesn't matter!
When two Masters clash like this,

164
00:09:31,520 --> 00:09:33,180
it's bound to be an epic, heart-stopping battle.

165
00:09:33,640 --> 00:09:34,620
I can't wait!

166
00:09:35,560 --> 00:09:37,980
Hey, you two better not be rooting for the wrong side.

167
00:09:41,800 --> 00:09:42,710
Forget it. It's about to start.

168
00:09:52,360 --> 00:09:54,780
If my Speed Dragon Yo-Yo is considered
the 2nd-best in the world,

169
00:09:55,720 --> 00:09:56,700
then no one would dare claim to be Number 1.

170
00:09:59,080 --> 00:10:01,020
And as for my Fire Warrior Yo-Yo... starting right now,

171
00:10:02,440 --> 00:10:03,310
it will never be a Runner-Up again.

172
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:07,260
Bring it on.

173
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:16,000
[Name: Leo | Team: Jianghai]
[Yo-Yo: Fire Warrior | Special Move: Crimson Holy Light]

174
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:22,000
[Name: Mark | Team: Jianghai Captain]
[Yo-Yo: Speed Dragon | Special Move: Golden Dragon Tail Whip]

175
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,960
Captain, use your Signature Move!

176
00:12:32,460 --> 00:12:33,460
Golden Dragon Tail Whip

177
00:12:33,620 --> 00:12:34,720
Eclipse.

178
00:12:52,000 --> 00:12:53,000
Yay!

179
00:12:55,720 --> 00:12:56,420
Leo wins!

180
00:13:00,040 --> 00:13:02,460
Leo, that Eclipse move of yours was absolutely insane!

181
00:13:02,920 --> 00:13:04,860
Your speed was incredible. I was totally stunned.

182
00:13:05,320 --> 00:13:06,780
I love the name "Eclipse."

183
00:13:07,240 --> 00:13:08,220
That's so superficial.

184
00:13:10,120 --> 00:13:11,580
That kind of Power requires incredible inner strength.

185
00:13:13,960 --> 00:13:14,940
So childish.

186
00:13:15,880 --> 00:13:18,090
You're still a long way from reaching
the highest level of Yo-Yo mastery.

187
00:13:20,680 --> 00:13:21,180
We're not done yet!

188
00:13:23,080 --> 00:13:23,730
Let's go 1 more round!

189
00:13:24,500 --> 00:13:25,500
Whatever.

190
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,380
Captain, we've got your back!

191
00:13:29,220 --> 00:13:29,970
What are you doing?!

192
00:13:37,280 --> 00:13:38,940
Mark! You're the Captain!

193
00:13:39,680 --> 00:13:41,340
How could you instigate a private duel like this?

194
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,260
Get back to Camp right now!

195
00:14:17,320 --> 00:14:19,260
Leo, get over to the Training Field. Now.

196
00:14:20,200 --> 00:14:21,660
You're going to be punished right alongside Mark.

197
00:14:23,560 --> 00:14:24,540
Your punishment is that:

198
00:14:25,180 --> 00:14:27,420
You'll both perform 30
Fundamental Yo-Yo drills, 20 times each.

199
00:14:28,360 --> 00:14:28,860
No breaks in between.

200
00:14:33,820 --> 00:14:34,620
Why?

201
00:14:35,080 --> 00:14:36,280
Only the Loser should be punished!

202
00:14:37,760 --> 00:14:38,460
Who said that?

203
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,780
Anyone who goes behind the Coach's back,
breaks the rules,

204
00:14:43,420 --> 00:14:44,620
and fights a private Duel

205
00:14:45,640 --> 00:14:46,990
will be punished, regardless of who wins or loses!

206
00:15:03,400 --> 00:15:03,900
Stop!

207
00:15:05,800 --> 00:15:07,260
First, I want you two standing face-to-face.

208
00:15:08,200 --> 00:15:09,970
Now shake hands and make up.

209
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,500
Shake hands immediately

210
00:15:19,140 --> 00:15:19,740
What kind of attitude is that?

211
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:21,580
Shake hands again!

212
00:15:39,880 --> 00:15:41,340
Watching Masters duel is just the best.

213
00:15:42,280 --> 00:15:43,260
With skills like Leo's,

214
00:15:43,720 --> 00:15:46,620
why didn't he show us what he could do sooner?

215
00:15:47,080 --> 00:15:48,460
Leo's just not the type of guy

216
00:15:48,520 --> 00:15:49,500
who likes to show off.

217
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,900
If the Coach hadn't stepped in

218
00:15:52,540 --> 00:15:53,580
and let them go one more round,

219
00:15:54,280 --> 00:15:56,700
Mickey, do you think Leo would've won again?

220
00:15:56,960 --> 00:15:57,630
Of course he would've!

221
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:01,450
That's hard to say. Don't forget,

222
00:16:01,480 --> 00:16:04,860
Mark was the Champion of our
District Tournament last year.

223
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:06,780
Let me tell you something.

224
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:09,180
Leo's skill level is way beyond what you can imagine.

225
00:16:09,640 --> 00:16:11,580
I saw him do "Discs Fill the Sky" with my own eyes.

226
00:16:12,600 --> 00:16:13,980
What kind of move is that?

227
00:16:15,200 --> 00:16:16,380
Never heard of it, right?

228
00:16:16,540 --> 00:16:18,300
It's a variation of "Ferris Flying Saucer!"

229
00:16:19,040 --> 00:16:20,700
I'd only ever read about it in books before.

230
00:16:21,160 --> 00:16:23,100
I didn't think anyone could actually pull it off.

231
00:16:23,360 --> 00:16:25,020
But then Leo went and did it.

232
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:28,250
Wow! What an effect it had?

233
00:16:30,360 --> 00:16:31,740
What effect? Tell me!

234
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,140
You wouldn't even believe me if I told you.

235
00:16:35,560 --> 00:16:37,500
Chuck, go get some water!

236
00:16:37,960 --> 00:16:39,420
Hold on. Mickey, spill it!

237
00:16:40,160 --> 00:16:41,340
It was insane!

238
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:43,740
After he did it, for several minutes,

239
00:16:44,200 --> 00:16:45,180
we couldn't hear a thing.

240
00:16:45,640 --> 00:16:46,450
We completely lost our hearing.

241
00:16:47,440 --> 00:16:49,020
No way. Why?

242
00:16:49,480 --> 00:16:51,420
Because it was so fast! The books say it

243
00:16:51,500 --> 00:16:53,820
transcends normal speed and sensory perception.

244
00:16:54,560 --> 00:16:55,740
It renders your sight and hearing

245
00:16:56,100 --> 00:16:57,660
completely useless.

246
00:16:58,120 --> 00:17:00,550
Hearing that just makes my hair stand up.

247
00:17:01,560 --> 00:17:03,420
I was standing there with my mouth hanging wide open,

248
00:17:03,840 --> 00:17:05,090
like my jaw was about to hit the floor.

249
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:08,750
Chuck, hurry up and get the water!

250
00:17:09,520 --> 00:17:10,620
We're all out of water here!

251
00:17:11,560 --> 00:17:13,020
Can't you see we're in the middle of something important?

252
00:17:13,480 --> 00:17:14,940
You guys can go get water, too.

253
00:17:16,360 --> 00:17:18,980
Chuck is happy to help out everyone. What's it to you?

254
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:22,620
Chuck, don't listen to him blowing smoke. Just go.

255
00:17:24,320 --> 00:17:25,500
Chuck, ignore them.

256
00:17:26,440 --> 00:17:27,900
Just 'cause he's tight with the Captain,

257
00:17:28,160 --> 00:17:29,340
he thinks he can boss everyone around.

258
00:17:29,800 --> 00:17:30,780
What's so special about him?

259
00:17:32,200 --> 00:17:35,100
Even if you wanted to get on the Captain's good side,
he wouldn't give you the time of day.

260
00:17:35,560 --> 00:17:36,540
I wouldn't want to anyway.

261
00:17:37,280 --> 00:17:39,870
If Leo had just shown off his
Skills in front of the Coach sooner,

262
00:17:39,880 --> 00:17:42,300
Mark never would've become Captain in the first place.

263
00:17:43,040 --> 00:17:44,700
You little punk, you've got some nerve.

264
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:46,620
How dare you attack the Captain like that!

265
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,060
I'm just stating the facts.

266
00:17:48,520 --> 00:17:49,500
The Captain's position should go to

267
00:17:49,560 --> 00:17:50,640
whoever has the best skills

268
00:17:51,580 --> 00:17:52,380
Right, Chuck?

269
00:17:53,120 --> 00:17:54,780
Come on, let's go find Leo!

270
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:55,740
Chuck!

271
00:17:57,060 --> 00:17:59,580
Chuck, don't you want to see
"Discs Fill the Sky"? Let's go!

272
00:18:17,800 --> 00:18:18,300
As the Captain,

273
00:18:18,760 --> 00:18:20,700
you should prioritize the unity of the entire Team above all else.

274
00:18:21,640 --> 00:18:23,580
Not go around forming cliques and dividing everyone.

275
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:25,020
I wasn't forming any cliques.

276
00:18:28,360 --> 00:18:29,340
This kind of Duel,

277
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:30,980
instigated out of pure ego and aggression,

278
00:18:31,800 --> 00:18:33,150
is incredibly damaging to Team unity.

279
00:18:33,160 --> 00:18:34,140
You understand?

280
00:18:36,020 --> 00:18:36,530
Got it.

281
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:39,900
You are Teammates...

282
00:18:40,840 --> 00:18:42,780
It doesn't even matter who has the best skills.

283
00:18:43,240 --> 00:18:44,700
Don't get caught up fighting over meaningless pride.

284
00:18:45,620 --> 00:18:48,030
Think about it. No matter who's the most skilled,

285
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:49,980
it's only going to benefit
the Jianghai Team in the long run.

286
00:18:50,920 --> 00:18:51,900
As the Captain,

287
00:18:52,060 --> 00:18:54,300
you need to have the mindset of
looking at the bigger picture.

288
00:18:56,680 --> 00:18:59,100
No matter who it is, you should
be encouraging and helping them,

289
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:02,460
not pushing them away or suppressing them. Right?

290
00:19:15,880 --> 00:19:17,340
Leo, your skills are just on another level.

291
00:19:17,800 --> 00:19:19,260
If only you'd come along sooner.

292
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:20,900
What difference would it make?

293
00:19:21,160 --> 00:19:23,100
If you'd been here earlier,
you would've been our Captain for sure!

294
00:19:24,040 --> 00:19:25,500
I think if Leo had been here from the start

295
00:19:25,760 --> 00:19:27,390
and shown off his skills during the Team tryouts,

296
00:19:27,400 --> 00:19:28,860
the whole School would've been blown away.

297
00:19:29,020 --> 00:19:30,600
And Mark, who was one of the Judges,

298
00:19:30,760 --> 00:19:32,220
would've been totally humiliated.

299
00:19:32,760 --> 00:19:34,140
Don't talk nonsense.

300
00:19:34,200 --> 00:19:35,700
What's there to be afraid of?

301
00:19:49,000 --> 00:19:49,980
That scared me!

302
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,860
Leo, it would be so awesome if you were the Captain.

303
00:19:53,800 --> 00:19:55,260
Can we go suggest that to the Coach?

304
00:19:56,200 --> 00:19:57,180
Don't fight over this.

305
00:19:57,640 --> 00:19:58,620
I don't care about being Captain or not.

306
00:19:59,080 --> 00:20:00,990
What's most important right now
is improving my Yo-Yo skills.

307
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:20,000
1, 2, 3, 4!

308
00:20:25,960 --> 00:20:26,460
Halt!

309
00:20:27,880 --> 00:20:28,860
Face straight!

310
00:20:29,800 --> 00:20:30,700
Dress left!

311
00:20:34,120 --> 00:20:34,620
Eyes front!

312
00:20:35,560 --> 00:20:36,060
Breakfast time!

313
00:20:39,000 --> 00:20:40,000
Listen up.

314
00:20:43,720 --> 00:20:45,180
We still have to keep practicing.

315
00:20:45,640 --> 00:20:49,020
Coach, I haven't even had breakfast yet!

316
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,940
The next Training Activity is...

317
00:20:51,880 --> 00:20:53,340
a 1-day trip to the Ancient Town!

318
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:57,180
Coach, are you talking in your sleep?

319
00:20:58,200 --> 00:20:59,580
You must have said the wrong thing.

320
00:21:00,040 --> 00:21:01,020
Do you think I'm like you?

321
00:21:02,920 --> 00:21:04,380
We need to balance work and rest.

322
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:06,780
So today, I'm giving you guys the day off.

323
00:21:07,240 --> 00:21:09,150
We're heading to the Ancient Town next to Falcon Camp

324
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:11,500
for a full day of fun. How's that sound?

325
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,060
Yay!

326
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:13,500
Coach, you're a genius!

327
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:14,940
Long live the Coach!

328
00:21:15,400 --> 00:21:16,380
Coach, we'll love you forever!

329
00:21:17,000 --> 00:21:18,000
Hey.

330
00:21:19,040 --> 00:21:20,220
Now that's just getting weird.

331
00:21:21,640 --> 00:21:22,620
Alright, breakfast time!

